What are Heavy Alkyl Benzenes (HAB)?
Heavy Alkyl Benzenes (HAB) are chemical compounds produced as a byproduct during the manufacturing of Linear Alkyl Benzene (LAB) and Branched Alkyl Benzene (BAB). Primarily composed of dialkyl benzenes, HAB is characterized as a yellow, oily material with low viscosity. It serves as a crucial raw material and performance additive, mainly used in the formulation of lubricant additives, base oils for lubricants, and heat conduction oils.
